shairport-sync: add a libgcrypt crypto backend (--with-ssl=gcrypt)

Lets shairport-sync build without OpenSSL or Mbed TLS. libgcrypt already
provides the AirPlay 2 pairing crypto (pair_ap); this adds the rest:
  - common.c: base64, and RSA from the built-in PKCS#1 key (PKCS#1 v1.5 raw
    signature for Apple-Challenge, RSA-OAEP/SHA-1 key decryption)
  - player.c: AES-128-CBC decryption of classic AirPlay audio
  - rtsp.c, shairport.c, metadata/hub.c: MD5 (digest auth, device UUID,
    cover-art file names)
Applies to shairport-sync 0a34fbda83724cc06266aadcf7c88acc8fef4e7d (5.6.2).

